 1. "set" in dir(builtins), type(set()), type({})                    [True, 'set', 'dict']
 2. hasattr(set.add, "__code__")  (built in: no Python source)       False
 3. {3, 1, 2}, set([3, 1]), frozenset(range(1, 4))                   [{1, 2, 3}, {1, 3}, frozenset({1, 2, 3})]
 4. list({3, 1, 2}); after discard(1), add(1); list({8, 1})          [[1, 2, 3], [1, 2, 3], [8, 1]]
 5. s = {1, 2}; s.add(3) (returns None); 3 in s; s.add(4)            [None, True, None]
 6. {1, 2} | {2, 3}, &, -, ^                                         [{1, 2, 3}, {2}, {1}, {1, 3}]
 7. {1} <= {1, 2}, issubset, <, {1}.isdisjoint({2})                  [True, True, True, True]
 8. {1, 2} == {2, 1}; {{1}}; {frozenset({1})}; frozenset({1}) == {1} [True, TypeError, True, True]
 9. 2 in {1, 2}; match 2: case x if x in {1, 2}                      [True, 'in']
10. comprehension, filter, sorted, | : the type each returns         ['set', 'list', 'list', 'set']
11. s.discard(9) (returns None, no error), s.remove(9)               [None, KeyError]
12. frozenset({1}).add(2)                                            AttributeError
13. len({x, x'}) for Plain, ByValue (__eq__+__hash__), EqOnly        [2, 1, 'TypeError']
14. {[1, 2]}; (1, 2) in {(1, 2)}; len and repr of {1, 1.0, True}     [TypeError, True, 1, {1}]
15. a list is refused at insertion (row 14): no stale element        -
16. no sorted set: sorted(s), or bisect.bisect([1, 3, 5], 4)         [[1, 2, 3], 2]
17. sorted(set("hello")), list(dict.fromkeys("hello"))               [['e', 'h', 'l', 'o'], ['h', 'e', 'l', 'o']]
18. {1, 2} < {1, 2, 3}, {1} < {2}, {1} > {2}  (no <=>)               [True, False, False]
